						<Class name="AZStd::string" field="Text" value="The field below displays the localized value of the localization key &lt;i&gt;&amp;#64;ui_Hello&lt;/i&gt; for the current language.\n\nWhen the language changes, the font family that's being used will automatically switch font assets to render the characters of that language.\n\nAt &lt;b&gt;runtime&lt;/b&gt;, the current language is given by the &lt;i&gt;g_language&lt;/i&gt; console variable. Language-specific assets are loaded from their associated PAK files. Otherwise, the &lt;i&gt;sys_localization_folder&lt;/i&gt; console variable specifies where to load 'loose' language-specific assets from.\n\nIn the &lt;b&gt;UI Editor&lt;/b&gt;, you can change languages via the &lt;i&gt;Set Current Language&lt;/i&gt; menu option.
